sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Alice as Alice (Client A)
    participant WS as WebSocket Gateway
    participant KMS as Envelope Encryption Service
    participant DB as MongoDB (chat_messages)
    actor Bob as Bob (Client B)

    Alice->>WS: Send Message Payload {conv_id, recipient, text}
    WS->>WS: Authorize conversation participation
    WS->>KMS: Encrypt (plaintext, entity_type="chat", entity_id=conv_id)
    KMS->>KMS: Derive DEK via HKDF-SHA256 (MasterKey + conv_id context)
    KMS->>KMS: Encrypt with AES-256-GCM (Generates Nonce + 128-bit Auth Tag)
    KMS-->>WS: Return Ciphertext + Nonce + Tag + KeyVersion ("v2")
    
    WS->>DB: Save to database (Only encrypted ciphertext stored)
    DB-->>WS: Write Confirmed
    
    WS->>Bob: Push realtime payload via WebSocket (Decrypted on flight / secure channel)
    Bob-->>WS: Acknowledge Receipt
    WS-->>Alice: Delivery Acknowledgment (Checkmark updated)

    Note over DB,KMS: Ciphertext Transplant Attack Defense
    Note over DB,KMS: If attacker copies ciphertext to another conversation,<br/>HKDF info mismatch causes AES-GCM tag verification failure.
